From: richie-rich90454 <rjiang880@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 0004/0014] Remove all telemetry

This patch removes all outbound telemetry from the workbench.

Rationale: VS Code ships Azure Application Insights telemetry to
Microsoft. A self-hosted IDE must not send data outside the workspace.

Touches:
  - product.json (enableTelemetry, aiConfig, crashReporter)
  - src/vs/platform/telemetry/ (TelemetryService registration)
  - src/vs/workbench/services/telemetry/ (TelemetryService registration)
  - vendor/vscode-telemetry (replaced with no-op)
  - vendor/vscode-telemetry-workbench (replaced with no-op)

Removal steps:
  1. Replace vscode-telemetry with a no-op module.
  2. Replace @vscode/telemetry with a no-op.
  3. Patch product.json: remove aiConfig, set enableTelemetry false,
     remove telemetryOptOutUrl and crashReporter.
  4. Patch src/vs/platform/telemetry/ to no-op implementations.
  5. Patch src/vs/workbench/services/telemetry/ similarly.
  6. Disable ExperimentsService by removing its registration.
  7. Remove the update endpoint and UpdateService checks.
  8. Force telemetryLevel read-only off.

Diff: authored on the upstream checkout (see build.sh).
Verification: ide/tests/no-network-test/ asserts no outbound connections.
